; NextDAAD SP16 Task 7 fixture - the AY characterization ladder, the
; STOPM repro and the BEEP scale.
;
; Compiled by tests\build-tests.ps1 on every run; staged as the active
; sd\GAME.DDB by tests\build-tests.ps1 -AudLad, which also stages the
; five ladder songs generated by tests\audio\mkladder.py as sd\001.AKY
; .. sd\005.AKY plus sd\GAME.AKY (a BYTE-IDENTICAL copy of 001.AKY -
; see the STOPM section below for why that matters).
;
; Owner leg instructions are EAR CARDS #T7A / #T7B / #T7C / #T7D in the
; SP16 Task 7 report. Nothing in this fixture judges audio quality -
; the interpreter cannot hear. Every verb here exists to put ONE known
; stimulus on the AY and stop.
;
; THE LADDER (#T7A). Five songs with strictly nested content: rung N's
; channels 1..N are byte-identical to rung M's channels 1..N. Only the
; number of sounding voices (and therefore of sounding PSGs) changes.
;   LAD1 -> 001.AKY  1 channel   (PSG 1 only)
;   LAD3 -> 002.AKY  3 channels  (PSG 1 full)
;   LAD6 -> 003.AKY  6 channels  (PSG 1 + PSG 2)
;   LAD9 -> 004.AKY  9 channels  (all three PSGs)
;   LADQ -> 005.AKY  9 channels at volume 5 instead of 11
; LADQ is the discriminator: if LAD9 is distorted and LADQ is clean,
; the artifact is summing level, not channel count or PSG mixing.
;
; THE STOPM REPRO (#T7B). sd\GAME.AKY is a byte-identical copy of
; sd\001.AKY, so "autoplay -> STOPM -> LAD1" plays the SAME BYTES
; twice. Any pitch difference between the two is therefore interpreter
; or hardware state, never a difference in the material - which is
; exactly the confound the original 2026-07-23 sighting could not
; exclude (the tune that autoplayed and the tune MUSIC restarted were
; different files).
;
; THE BEEP SCALE (#T7C). Task 1 changed BEEP's parameter order (arg1 =
; tone, arg2 = duration in centiseconds) and raised the pitch ceiling
; to 238, so tones 224-238 sound here for the first time. BEEPS walks
; a C major scale and then the whole new top octave; ORDER plays one
; long low note followed by one short high note, which is audibly
; wrong in both dimensions if the parameter order ever regresses.

; System flags used by name (DAAD BLANK template spellings)
#define fPlayer             38
#define fDarkF              28

/CTL
_
/VOC
NORTH  2  noun
SOUTH  3  noun
LOOK   4  verb
LAD1   60 verb
LAD3   61 verb
LAD6   62 verb
LAD9   63 verb
LADQ   64 verb
STOPM  65 verb
BEEPS  66 verb
ORDER  67 verb
/STX
/0  "It's too dark to see anything."
/1  "I can also see:"
/2  "What now?"
/3  "What next?"
/4  "What should I do now?"
/5  "What should I do next?"
/6  "I didn't understand."
/7  "I can't go in that direction."
/8  "I can't do that."
/9  "I have with me:"
/10 "I am wearing:"
/11 " "
/12 "Are you sure?"
/13 "Another go?"
/14 " "
/15 "OK."
/16 "Press any key."
/17 " "
/18 " "
/19 " "
/20 " "
/21 " "
/22 " "
/23 "I'm not wearing one of those."
/24 "I can't. My hands are full."
/25 "I already have the _."
/26 "There isn't one of those here."
/27 "I can't carry any more things."
/28 "I don't have one of those."
/29 "I'm already wearing the _."
/30 "Y"
/31 "N"
/32 "More..."
/33 ">"
/34 " "
/35 " "
/36 "I now have the _."
/37 "I'm now wearing the _."
/38 "I've removed the _."
/39 "I've dropped the _."
/40 "I can't wear the _."
/41 "I can't remove the _."
/42 "I can't remove the _. My hands are full."
/43 "The _ weighs too much for me."
/44 "The _ is in the"
/45 "The _ isn't in the"
/46 ", "
/47 " and "
/48 ".#n"
/49 "I don't have the _."
/50 "I'm not wearing the _."
/51 "."
/52 "There isn't one of those in the"
/53 "Nothing."
/54 " "
/55 " "
/56 " "
/57 "I/O Error"
/58 " "
/59 "File name error."
/60 "Type in name of file."
/MTX
/0 "NEXTDAAD AY LADDER FIXTURE (SP16 TASK 7)#n"
/OTX
/0 "a brass lamp"
/LTX
/0 ""
/1 "The listening room."
/CON
/0
NORTH 1
/1
SOUTH 0
/OBJ
/0    1   1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   _ _
/PRO 0
> _ _   AT 0
        PROCESS 6
> _ _   WINDOW 1
        WINAT 0 0
        WINSIZE 25 127
        CLEAR fDarkF
> _ _   WINDOW 1
        DESC @fPlayer
> _ _   PROCESS 1
/PRO 1
> _ _   PARSE 0
        REDO
> _ _   PROCESS 5
        ISDONE
        REDO
> _ _   MOVE fPlayer
        CLS
        RESTART
> _ _   SYSMESS 8
        REDO
/PRO 5
; ---- the channel-count ladder (EAR CARD #T7A) ----
; Every rung is SFX n 7 = load NNN.AKY and loop it. A rung that finds
; no file is a documented silent no-op, so a staging miss reads as
; silence, not as a distortion result - the card says to check the
; "playing" line before scoring a rung.
> LAD1 _  MES "rung 1: 001.AKY - 1 channel (PSG 1 A)#n"
          SFX 1 7
          DONE
> LAD3 _  MES "rung 2: 002.AKY - 3 channels (PSG 1)#n"
          SFX 2 7
          DONE
> LAD6 _  MES "rung 3: 003.AKY - 6 channels (PSG 1 + 2)#n"
          SFX 3 7
          DONE
> LAD9 _  MES "rung 4: 004.AKY - 9 channels (PSG 1 + 2 + 3)#n"
          SFX 4 7
          DONE
> LADQ _  MES "rung 4b: 005.AKY - 9 channels, volume 5 not 11#n"
          SFX 5 7
          DONE
; ---- STOPM (EAR CARD #T7B) ----
; GAME.AKY == 001.AKY byte for byte, so LAD1 after STOPM replays
; exactly what boot autoplayed.
> STOPM _ MES "music stopped#n"
          SFX 0 8
          DONE
; ---- the BEEP scale (EAR CARD #T7C) ----
; Tones are the jdaad pitch numbers: even, 24..238, index (tone-24)/2
; into the 108-entry equal-temperament table. 120 = C4.
; Durations are CENTISECONDS (Task 1 order: BEEP tone duration).
> BEEPS _ MES "BEEP C major scale from C4#n"
          BEEP 120 30
          BEEP 124 30
          BEEP 128 30
          BEEP 130 30
          BEEP 134 30
          BEEP 138 30
          BEEP 142 30
          BEEP 144 30
          MES "BEEP new top octave, tones 224-238#n"
          BEEP 224 30
          BEEP 226 30
          BEEP 228 30
          BEEP 230 30
          BEEP 232 30
          BEEP 234 30
          BEEP 236 30
          BEEP 238 30
          MES "BEEP scale done#n"
          DONE
; Parameter-order probe: one LOW note held ONE SECOND, then one HIGH
; note lasting a TENTH of one. Swap the arguments and the first would
; be a 1.2-second-ish silence-then-click at tone 100 and the second a
; long note - audibly different, in both dimensions, from this.
> ORDER _ MES "BEEP order: low+long (100 cs), then high+short (10 cs)#n"
          BEEP 100 100
          BEEP 220 10
          MES "BEEP order done#n"
          DONE
/PRO 6
> _ _   WINDOW 1
        WINAT 0 0
        WINSIZE 25 127
        PAPER 0
        INK 7
        CLS
        MESSAGE 0
> _ _   MES "Boot autoplay is GAME.AKY = 001.AKY (1 channel).#n#n"
        MES "LAD1 LAD3 LAD6 LAD9 LADQ  channel-count ladder#n"
        MES "STOPM                     stop the music#n"
        MES "BEEPS                     BEEP scale + new top octave#n"
        MES "ORDER                     BEEP parameter-order probe#n#n"
        MES "Cards #T7A #T7B #T7C #T7D in the Task 7 report.#n"
        GOTO 1
/END
